<title>FRANCE: Suez Lyonnaise unit posts gain on Sephora sale.</title>
<headline>Suez Lyonnaise unit posts gain on Sephora sale.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-07-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Suez-Lyonnaise des Eaux said on Wednesday its Suez Industrie unit realised a 400 million franc capital gain from the sale of its 30 percent stake in Sephora to LVMH Moet Hennessy Louis Vuitton.</p>
<p>LVMH said earlier it had bought Sephora, France's leading perfume and beauty products retailer, for 1.6 billion francs ($260.8 million).</p>
<p>Suez-Lyonnaise said it sold its stake in Sephora as part of the LVMH deal.</p>
<p>Suez-Lyonnaise also said its 20-percent owned Eurosuez fund, which held a part of Sephora, earned a 200 million franc capital gain from selling its stake.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom +331 4221 5452</p>
